WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:01.980
- [Reporter] Chinese fighter jets

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.480
carried out simulated attacks

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.850
as they flew near Taiwan's airspace,

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.400
warships sailed close to
the island's military bases

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.190
and major ports, and
long range rockets flew

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.830
in the direction of the
self-ruled democracy.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.270
All this was part of war games

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:18.303
following House Speaker Nancy
Pelosi's visit to Taipei.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.090
To understand what China's army is doing,

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.100
military analysts have
been looking at footage

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.260
from state media and mapping the locations

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.360
where the drills have taken place.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.120
Beijing sees Taiwan as
part of its own territory,

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.590
and with these military drills,

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.870
it's showing how it would
seek to isolate the island

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.433
in the event of a conflict.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.343
These are six zones

00:00:37.343 --> 00:00:39.690
where the Chinese People's Liberation Army

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.630
has been holding its
exercises in recent days.

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:47.220
- China appears to be
practicing its ability

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.960
to enforce a blockade in
Taiwan by putting its ships

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.220
and planes basically in a
big circle around Taiwan.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.053
- [Reporter] During the drills,

00:00:57.053 --> 00:00:59.100
China showed that different
branches of its army

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.600
can work in sync.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.090
- China's clearly trying to show

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:07.380
that it can operate in
various regions around Taiwan.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.050
It can coordinate that large military

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:13.710
across the seas and the
air and with its missiles

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:17.040
and its intelligence
gathering its communication,

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.987
its reconnaissance.

00:01:18.987 --> 00:01:20.370
- [Reporter] But the drills also showed

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:22.710
that Beijing's military has limitations.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:25.800
Military analysts say that
China appears to lack the assets

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.230
to impose a total blockade of the island,

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.180
so instead, it seems to be preparing

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.430
for a sort of quarantine around Taiwan.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:36.510
- A mini blockade of
Taiwan, cutting off aspects

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.120
of its connections with
the rest of the world,

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.580
allowing Taiwan to import food

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:45.240
but not allowing it to
bring in other materials;

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.830
for instance, oil.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:47.663
- [Reporter] Looking closer

00:01:47.663 --> 00:01:49.260
at where some of the zones were set up

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:51.600
shows how China could
choke off the island.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.190
This zone located north of Taiwan

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:55.380
is just some 30 miles away from Taipei,

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.740
which is home to the island's
busiest international airport.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:01:59.850
And this southwest zone

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.970
is near Taiwan's most
important commercial port.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.470
And then there's the Taiwan Strait,

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.780
one of the busiest trade
routes in the world.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.040
The proximity of the action

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.870
to key shipping routes in the region

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:11.880
triggered the delays of
some commercial flights

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.740
and shipments, demonstrating the pain

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.380
China could also inflict
on world commerce.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:20.970
- This is a very active area
for shipping, connecting Korea

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:24.060
and Japan with the oil
markets of the Middle East,

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.610
connecting the semiconductor industry

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.317
with the rest of the world.

00:02:28.317 --> 00:02:29.790
- [Reporter] The drills also took place

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.340
in parts of Japan's
exclusive economic zone,

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.470
an area of the sea that
gives sovereign states

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:37.470
the rights to exploit and
control marine resources.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:38.940
Japan's defense minister says

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:41.310
some of China's missiles landed there.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:46.310
- If there is a Chinese
live-fire exercise in those seas,

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.600
commercial ships will be deterred

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.233
and that will certainly
collapse trade in that area.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:54.330
- [Reporter] The Chinese military said

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.370
it would continue the drills around Taiwan

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.740
beyond the initially announced four days.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.210
So as tensions continue to mount,

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:02.460
the question is whether these exercises

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:05.280
would escalate larger military
activity in the region.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.980
- Any sustained effort like we've seen

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.680
with these exercises
is clearly gonna result

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:15.510
in more military activity by
the US, possibly by Japan,

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:17.227
and other powers in the region.

00:03:17.227 --> 00:03:20.144
(soft tense music)

